CHECK:ARCH_INCLUDE_LINUX: Consider using #include <linux/cacheflush.h> instead of <asm/cacheflush.h>
#188: FILE: arch/x86/mm/tlb.c:16:
+#include <asm/cacheflush.h>

Whenever asm/file.h is included and linux/file.h exists, a
conversion can be made when linux/file.h includes asm/file.h.
However this is not always the case (See signal.h).
This message type is emitted only for includes from arch/.

CHECK:COMPARISON_TO_NULL: Comparison to NULL could be written "!tsk"
#256: FILE: arch/x86/mm/tlb.c:215:
